From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Wallpaper & style shows NickelOS's wallpapers

Wallpaper & style's collections came from Google's servers (Backdrop).
They are NickelOS's own wallpapers now (Dresden, 2026-11-04): one
collection, "NickelOS", of the pictures in the image at
/usr/share/chromeos-assets/wallpaper/nickel (chromeos-bsp-nickel), listed
in its collection.json, so pictures change without a new Chrome. A picture
with a dark-mode twin (the default wave) is one unit of a light and a dark
image, which ChromeOS switches with the color mode, as it does for Google's.
"Surprise me" picks one of them.

Their addresses are chrome://personalization/nickel-wallpaper/NAME.jpg.
The app's request filter serves a thumbnail there (thumbs/NAME.jpg), and
WallpaperImageDownloader reads the picture itself from disk for that
address, where it asked Google's servers for an online wallpaper at twice
the screen's size. Names are checked before either touches a file.

---
